## Predictive nodes (anomaly / forecast — ml-vision.md step 3)
flows-palette-anomaly = Anomaly detection
flows-palette-anomaly-help = Flag unusual values of a measurement (spike, drop, regime change) without a fixed threshold
flows-palette-forecast = Forecast
flows-palette-forecast-help = Forecast a measurement and predict when it will cross a threshold (wear, fouling, drift)
flows-predict-port-detail = detail
flows-anomaly-port-flag = anomaly
flows-forecast-port-breach = breach
flows-forecast-port-eta = eta (s)
flows-anomaly-help = Scores each value against the recent history of its series (one series per message topic). Warms up first, then flags what does not look like the usual behavior.
flows-anomaly-method = Method
flows-anomaly-method-robust-z = Outlier (robust z-score)
flows-anomaly-method-robust-z-help = Distance to the median in robust standard deviations. No model, resistant to the outliers it looks for: the safe default.
flows-anomaly-method-forecast-band = Out of forecast band
flows-anomaly-method-forecast-band-help = Predicts the next value (exponential smoothing, with seasonality if set) and flags values outside the confidence band. Follows trends and daily cycles.
flows-anomaly-method-changepoint = Regime change
flows-anomaly-method-changepoint-help = Detects when the series changes level or variability (after a failure, an intervention, a setting change). Fires once per change.
flows-predict-key = Value key
flows-predict-key-hint = Field of an object payload; leave empty when the payload is the number itself.
flows-predict-window = Window (samples)
flows-predict-window-hint = History kept per series: { $min } to { $max }. Survives redeploys.
flows-predict-min-samples = Warm-up (samples)
flows-predict-min-samples-hint = Samples collected before the first result (at least { $min }).
flows-anomaly-threshold = Threshold (robust z)
flows-anomaly-threshold-hint = 3.5 is a common choice; lower = more sensitive.
flows-predict-level = Confidence level
flows-predict-level-hint = Between 0.5 and 0.999 (e.g. 0.95).
flows-predict-season = Season (samples)
flows-predict-season-hint = Samples per cycle (e.g. 24 for hourly data with a daily cycle); 0 = none.
flows-anomaly-hazard = Expected run length
flows-anomaly-hazard-hint = Typical number of samples between two changes; higher = fewer, clearer detections.
flows-anomaly-ports-help = Outputs: detail (value, score, expected band), then anomaly (true / false) — wire it to a notification trigger.
flows-forecast-help = Forecasts the next values of a series (one series per message topic). With a threshold, predicts when it will be crossed.
flows-forecast-model = Model
flows-forecast-model-ets = Exponential smoothing (trend, seasonality)
flows-forecast-model-linear = Linear trend (slow drift, wear)
flows-forecast-horizon = Horizon (steps)
flows-forecast-horizon-hint = Steps forecast ahead (one step = the usual time between samples), up to { $max }.
flows-forecast-horizon-span = Horizon ≈ { $at_1hz } at one sample per second, { $at_1min } at one sample per minute. For a slow drift (wear, clogging), feed a slower series (e.g. a per-minute average) rather than raw 1 Hz samples.
flows-forecast-threshold = Threshold
flows-forecast-threshold-hint = Optional: breach level to watch.
flows-forecast-direction = Breach when
flows-forecast-direction-above = above the threshold
flows-forecast-direction-below = below the threshold
flows-forecast-every = Refit every (samples)
flows-forecast-every-hint = 1 = at every sample; raise it for fast series.
flows-forecast-ports-help = Outputs: detail (forecast points with bands, breach time), then breach (true / false) for a notification trigger, then seconds before the predicted breach.
err-predict-window-invalid = The window must be between 16 and 5000 samples
err-predict-min-samples-invalid = The warm-up must be between 8 samples and the window size
err-anomaly-threshold-invalid = The threshold must be a positive number
err-predict-level-invalid = The confidence level must be between 0.5 and 0.999
err-anomaly-hazard-invalid = The expected run length must be at least 2 samples
err-predict-season-invalid = The season must be 0 or at least 2 samples, with a warm-up of two full seasons
err-forecast-horizon-invalid = The horizon must be between 1 and 1000 steps
err-forecast-threshold-invalid = The threshold must be a number
err-forecast-every-invalid = The refit period must be between 1 and 1000 samples

