## Ontology errors (D176–D191)
err-ontology-not-found = Not found in the organization's ontology: it may have been archived or deleted.
err-ontology-already-exists = This already exists (same type key, or the same link is already open).
err-ontology-version-conflict = Someone changed it in the meantime (version { $current }): reload, then redo your change.
err-ontology-type-in-use = This type is still in use (live objects, references or links): archive them or remove the references first.
err-ontology-write-forbidden = Your role cannot change objects of this type.
err-ontology-system-read-only = System types and objects are edited from their own pages (devices, media, flows…).
err-ontology-link-not-allowed = This link type does not connect objects of these types.
err-ontology-link-cardinality = An open link already takes this place: close it first (for example when replacing a sensor).
err-ontology-action-no-flow = No deployed flow handles this action: add an "Action trigger" node for it in a flow, then deploy the flow.
err-ontology-action-unavailable = The action bus (Valkey) is unavailable: the action was not sent.
err-ontology-changes-unavailable = History unavailable (OpenObserve not configured or unreachable).
err-ontology-action-unknown = The action { $action } of type { $object_type } does not exist in the organization's ontology: pick another one in the node.
err-media-diff-unsupported = Only documents whose text can be read are compared (text, Markdown, CSV, Word, PDF, sheets).
err-ext-no-agent = Waiting for a browser agent of the organization to be online.
err-crawl-blocked = The site refused the crawler (access denied or too many requests): the crawl stopped and never insists.
err-crawl-robots-disallowed = The site's robots.txt forbids crawling it: nothing was read. A browser agent can still capture pages by hand.
err-crawl-unreachable = The site cannot be reached (network, refused address or server error): the crawl will try again at the next round.
err-notify-dynamic-recipients-off = This node reads its recipient from the message: every channel must be an e-mail channel that allows recipients from flows (channel settings, owner or admin).
err-notify-dynamic-recipients-admin = Only owners and admins let a channel send to recipients read from flow messages.
err-ontology-node-unknown = This node names a type, a key or a link type that does not exist in the organization's ontology: pick another one in the node.
err-import-run-stale = This preview is out of date (already applied, or the import or the data changed): preview again.
err-import-run-interrupted = The import was interrupted (its server stopped): nothing was written, run the flow again.
err-import-has-errors = Some rows have errors: fix the file and preview it again before applying.
err-import-suspicious-drop = The source went from { $previous } to { $rows } records: the run was refused and nothing was closed.
err-import-schema-changed = The source changed shape (missing columns: { $columns }): nothing was written. Check the source, then adjust the column mapping.
err-import-source-unreachable = The source address cannot be reached (refused address, network or server error).
err-import-source-too-large = The source is too large: 200 MB once decompressed and 50,000 records per run at most.
err-import-source-unreadable = The file or the answer cannot be read in the expected format (CSV, Excel, JSON or XML).
err-ingest-staging-quota = The organisation's staging area is full (2 GB): nothing was downloaded. Wait for the purge or add a cleanup step at the end of the flow.
err-ingest-staging-unavailable = The staging storage cannot be reached: try again later.
err-ingest-no-resource = No resource of the dataset matches the pattern { $pattern }.
err-ingest-entry-missing = No file to read: no extracted entry matches { $entry }.
err-ingest-archive-unsupported = Unsupported archive format: zip, tar, tar.gz and gz only.
err-ingest-unsafe-path = The archive holds a path leaving its folder: refused.
err-ingest-suspicious-closures = This run would close { $closed } items out of { $held } (over { $max_pct } %): nothing was written. Check the source.
err-ontology-unique-duplicates = Several objects already share a value of { $property } ({ $values }): fix them before making it unique.
err-ontology-claim-unsourced = A claim is corroborated only with at least two pieces of distinct origins: link it to its sources ("is sourced by"), or write why in "Corroboration justification".
err-track-import-timezone-required = The file's times do not state their offset: choose the time zone of the recording.
err-track-import-empty = The file holds no usable point.
